{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"1f89901df1ea64fc25035684727808967ec7ee861371e9435d8dd6efeb673c45","digest":{"component_or_area":"git utility wrapper (gitutil.py)","key_entities":["src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py","run_git","tests/unit/test_run_git_wrapper.py","input_data","text","cwd","check","timeout","env"],"problem_keywords":["contract testing","git wrapper","input_data","text mode","bytes stdin","error handling","subprocess"],"propositions":["run_git lacks direct contract tests; its branches are only exercised through monkeypatched callers, leaving the real wrapper untested.","Calling run_git with bytes input_data and text=True (the default) raises an opaque AttributeError from subprocess instead of a clear, actionable error message.","A new direct contract matrix must validate that cwd=None omits -C prefix while a path-like cwd inserts -C <cwd> by observing git command behavior.","The run_git wrapper must guard the unsupported input_data=bytes + text=True combination and raise TypeError with a fix hint (binary stdin requires text=False).","Contract tests must verify check, timeout, env, and input_data (str) parameters behave correctly against a real temporary git repository."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785821544888409930,"uuid":"f543ee87-7834-4b7d-b2c9-23d2801b4df9"}